course: dictionary
lesson: 8299
title: The riverbed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A river is full of moving water, but the riverbed is the ground underneath it. Its name tells you what it is: a river's bed is the bottom that the water flows over. «Hippos cannot really swim or float; they walk along the riverbed» tells you that a riverbed is ground you can walk on.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «A platypus stuffs food from the riverbed into its cheek pouches» shows that food is found on the riverbed, so it is part of the river's bottom where small creatures live. «Fast-moving water can knock you off your feet even below the knee, and riverbeds are slippery» tells you what a riverbed feels like under your feet.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «they walk along the bottom of the river» in place of «they walk along the riverbed». If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A riverbed is the bottom of a river, the ground the water flows over.
fact: A riverbed can be made of stones, sand, mud and pebbles.
fact: In dry weather, a riverbed may be completely dry.
fact: Fossils and gold have been found in riverbeds, and water smooths the stones on them.
fact: «Riverbeds are slippery», so take care when you walk on them.
exercise: «Hippos ... walk along the riverbed.» Where do hippos walk? | *On the bottom of the river | In the sky | Inside their own shells | Up in the trees
exercise: What is a riverbed? | A boat that carries people across | The top of a waterfall | *The ground at the bottom of a river | A bridge that goes over a river
exercise: «Riverbeds are slippery.» What should you do when you walk on one? | Jump from stone to stone with your eyes shut | Lie down on the stones | *Take care and walk slowly | Run as fast as you can
test: In dry weather, what might a riverbed be? | A flat, grassy meadow | Higher than the trees | Full of fast-moving water | *Dry
test: Which of these has been found in riverbeds? | Clouds | Lighthouses | Birds' nests in trees | *Fossils and gold
exam: Which sentence uses riverbed correctly? | The riverbed was the name of a sweet we ate at the fair | *The children paddled along the stony riverbed, looking for pebbles | The riverbed was so high that we climbed up to the clouds | The riverbed was a tall tower with a flag on top
